Summary of the thesis:

Interactive AI-powered 3D avatar assistant built in Unity and integrated with the OpenAI API to provide intelligent conversation, voice interaction, and real-time facial animation.
The project combines artificial intelligence, speech recognition, text-to-speech synthesis, and a Ready Player Me avatar to create a dynamic and immersive virtual assistant experience.

The assistant is capable of listening to the user through speech-to-text using Unity’s DictationRecognizer, processing natural language requests via OpenAI models, and responding both visually and audibly using OpenAI’s text-to-speech system.
The generated speech is synchronized with the avatar’s facial blendshapes (jawOpen) to achieve real-time lip sync, creating a more natural and human-like interaction.

SakuraAI supports both voice and text input through a custom-built chat panel interface. Users can either speak to the avatar using a wake word system or type messages directly into the chat window.
The assistant processes requests using models such as GPT-4o and generates contextual, intelligent responses.
The system also includes logic to handle audio conflicts, automatic speech recognizer restarts, and synchronization between listening and speaking states to ensure stable operation.

The avatar is dynamically loaded using the Ready Player Me SDK, allowing customizable 3D characters.
Animations are controlled through a custom Animator Controller, and additional improvements have been implemented to reduce unnatural head movement and enhance idle behavior.
The project also features a minimalist, futuristic UI design to match the modern AI assistant concept.

When asked identity-related questions such as “Who are you?”, “What are you?”, or “Why were you made?”, the assistant is programmed to respond consistently with:
"I'm Personal Assistant made by Boguslav Pacyno to assist you in your work or have a chat."

The goal of SakuraAI is to create a personal AI assistant embodied in a realistic 3D avatar that can assist with tasks, hold natural conversations, present information, and provide engaging, human-like interaction.
The project demonstrates integration between Unity, real-time 3D animation systems, external AI APIs, voice technologies, and interactive UI systems.

Future development may include emotion-based facial expressions, improved animation blending during speech, memory-enhanced conversations, presentation narration mode, and multi-platform deployment.

SakuraAI represents a combination of AI engineering, real-time graphics, and interactive system design, showcasing how artificial intelligence can be embodied within a visually expressive digital character.
